                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "I'm not gonna front, if this game wasn't a dollar, when I came upon it, I very likely would NOT have even considered it. Having greatly enjoyed it since I played it, and considering it one of the most easy to understand, yet tough to master takes on Puzzle Fighter's puzzle methodology I've played in awhile, I maintain my original stance, for two primary reasons:\n\nA lack of compelling single player content\n\nAnd no native way to do online versus, which, considering it's THE ENTIRE POINT OF THE GAME, is kind of a big deal\n\nIf you're willing to jump through the Parsec hoops to make it happen, it's great fun, but the fact that is allows for 8 players, but ONLY allows for in person vs is SUCH a massive missed opportunity. Your enjoyment with this game will greatly depend on how much you're facing human competition, and not the INCREDIBLY UNFAIR AI players",
